  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nVISIT SOFO MUSEUM\nEverything you need to plan your day out\n\n \n\nSOFO Museum first opened during the summer of 2014, tucked away in the beautiful gardens in the grounds of The Oxfordshire Museum and Woodstock Library, and just on the doorstep of Blenheim Palace.\nMore than a local military museum, SOFO is a museum that everyone can enjoy, from kids to parents, and to grandparents. We tell stories of how conflict has affected the county and its people, from soldiers serving on the front lines to ordinary people living on the Home Front.\nOn top of a range of ever-changing displays and events, our permanent exhibits explore topics that you’ll find surprising and moving in equal measure, such as raw accounts of the liberation of Bergen-Belsen from both camp survivors and Oxfordshire soldiers. Battles of the Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry puts you on-board a Horsa Glider as it prepares to land in Normandy in the early hours of D-Day 1944, while Secret Agents, Secret Armies explores the real world of spies and espionage through the lens of Ian Fleming and James Bond\nSOFO holds a collection of over 3,500 objects and 7,500 archive items from two county regiments, the Queens Own Oxfordshire Hussars (QOOH) and the Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry. These are our starting point for reflecting on the county’s rich and diverse military heritage.\nWhat people say about us\nSOFO Museum is great day out, but don't just take our word for it...\nHidden Gem\n\n\"Hidden away in Woodstock but well worth a visit\"\n\n\"Undiscovered gem\"\n\n\"Cracking little museum\"\n\nTrip Advisor Reviews\n\nFamily Fun\n\n“great for all the family!”\n\n“grandchildren loved it”\n\n“a brilliant place to take a family”\n\nMore Facebook Reviews\n\nA Hit with History Buffs\n\n“A must for local historians”\n\n\"crammed with interesting militaria\"\n\n“A refreshingly interesting military museum”\n\nMore Google Reviews\n\nWhat's the best time to drop in?\nOur Opening Times\n\nTuesday - Saturday: 11am - 5pm\n\nSundays: 2pm - 5pm.\n\n(We don't 'do' Mondays!)\n\nHow long do you need to visit?\n\nWe recommend at least 1 hour to get the most from your visit\n\nLast Admission: 4.15pm (everyday)\n\nChanges to our normal opening times:\n\nMay Bank Holidays\n\nBH Monday 4 May 2026: Open 2pm – 5pm\nBH Monday 25 May 2026: Open 2pm – 5pm\n\nAutism Friendly Visits\n\nFor families with Special Educational Needs, including Autistic Spectrum Disorder, we can also open outside our regular hours. If you'd prefer to enjoy the Museum at a quieter time, without needing to worry about other visitors, and with many of the gallery sounds turned off, or our lighting dimmed. Explore our gallery spaces in peace, or get hands-on with our activities.\n\nPlease contact us for more information and to book. Children and young people under 18 go free; adults charged at standard admission rate.\n\nRegular times for these visits can be arranged each week from 10am - 11am on Saturdays in term time, or Wednesdays and Fridays during school holidays.\n\nContact us at education@sofo.org.uk to book and for more details.\n\nDownload a Dimensions Autism Friendly Social Story guide to the museum here or a copy of our gallery map here.\n\nBuying a ticket\nJust drop in, or book tickets in advance - it's up to you!\nAdmission Prices\n\nOne ticket, twelve months unlimited entry to all of our exhibitions.\n\nAdults: £9.00\n\nConcessions:  £8.00 (Seniors, Students, Armed Forces)\n\nChildren (5-16yrs) £5.50\n\nUnder 5s: Free\n\nCarers: Free\n\nFamily Tickets\n\n1 Adult, 2 Children: £15.00\n\n1 Adult, up to 4 Children: £20.00\n\n2 Adults, up to 4 Children: £28.00\n\nGift Aid: If you can make a Gift Aid donation, Soldiers of Oxfordshire Trust can reclaim an extra 25% on your ticket. It costs you nothing and goes directly towards the preservation of our collections.\n\nBook Online\n\nBook your admissions ahead of your visit via the TxGB Booking Portal\n\nBook Now\n\nFriends' Membership\n\nBecoming a Friend of the museum doesn't cost the world, and entitles you to a range of benefits - including free admission, exclusive events and invites, a copy of our guidebook, special offers and more!\n\nFind out more\n\nBlenheim Annual Pass Offer\nFree admission to the Main Gallery for visitors with a current and valid Blenheim Annual Pass.\nPlease bring your Annual and/or Privilege Passes with you to take advantage of the free admission offer.\n\nPlease note: Our free entry offer for Blenheim Annual Pass holders does not include entry to the Lee Miller exhibition, but all other galleries are included. Blenheim Annual Pass Holders can purchase discounted tickets (£5) to enter the  Lee Miller: A Woman at War exhibition.\n\nGoodJourney\nTravel a greener way for discounts! Enjoy 2for1 standard entry when you show a train or bus ticket from the day of your visit. Find out more about getting here car-free at GoodJourney.\nGetting Here\nWe're tucked away in Woodstock at the bottom of The Oxfordshire Museum's beautiful gardens, on the doorstep of Blenheim Palace's Woodstock Gate.\nWhere We Are\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum, Park Street, Woodstock, OX20 1SN\n\nWhere to Park\n\nWoodstock's free, Long Stay Car Park is on Hensington Road, a 10 minute walk from the museum.\n\nSat Nav: OX20 1JQ\n\nBlue Badge spaces and Pay and Display (1 - 5 hour) spaces can be found right outside the museum on Park Street\n\nBuses & Trains\n\nBuses:\n\nS3 and S7 from Oxford City Centre\n\nS7 from Witney\n\nNearest Train Stations:\n\nLong Hanborough (bus S7)\n\nOxford (bus S3 or S7)\n\nMore Useful Info\nGet A Gallery Map\n\nDownload (PDF)\n\nAccessibility Guide\n\nDownload (PDF)\n\nOur Customer Commitment\n\nDownload (PDF)\n\nNeed to get in touch?\nGive Us A Ring\n\n01993 810 210\n\nDrop Us An Email\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nSend A Letter\n\nSOFO Office, Harrisons Lane, Woodstock, OX20 1SS\n\nKeep in touch! Join our mailing list to stay up to date with SOFO news, events and exhibitions\n\nWelcome Guides\nTranslated Guides to SOFO Museum (PDF)\nUseful Links\nMore great stuff to see do in Woodstock and the surrounding area!\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
